{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/style/","title":"Typed styles","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"typed-styles","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Typed styles"}]},{"t":"callout","tone":"tip","caption":"The only way to style a component","children":[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"This section is "},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/style"},{"t":"text","text":": typed values, CSS emitted at build time, and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"a visual matrix you can enumerate. It costs a Vite plugin — see"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/style/setup","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Activating the style system"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — and a design system to declare. A"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"component's meta carries no CSS; see"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/components/styles","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Styling a component: the only way"}]},{"t":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/style"},{"t":"text","text":" makes a component's visual surface "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"derivable"}]},{"t":"text","text":" instead of"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"guessed. For any component you can ask what the exhaustive set of visual states"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"is, which of them are impossible, and whether the context it needs exists — and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the answers come from the same values the CSS is emitted from, not from a second"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"description that can drift."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"It buys that in three levels, and they do not adopt the same way."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"t":"text","text":"level"}],[{"t":"text","text":"what it gives you"}],[{"t":"text","text":"granularity of adoption"}]],"rows":[[[{"t":"text","text":"1 — tokens and typed variables"}],[{"t":"text","text":"no value is a string; no class is built at runtime"}],[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"one component at a time"}]},{"t":"text","text":""}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"2 — axes and the matrix"}],[{"t":"text","text":"the exhaustive list of visual states, with the drivers that reach them"}],[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"per component"}]},{"t":"text","text":""}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"3 — context obligations"}],[{"t":"text","text":"a missing scroll port, container or clipping ancestor fails the build"}],[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"per whole route"}]},{"t":"text","text":""}]]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Read that last column carefully, because it is the part that is easy to get"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"wrong. Level 3 is not a per-component guarantee: one unmigrated link in a route"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"and the requirement travels past it unanswered, so the compiler has nothing to"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"check. A partial level-3 adoption gives "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"zero"}]},{"t":"text","text":" of the guarantee, not most of"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"it — and the graph reports it rather than hiding it."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-rule-the-whole-thing-turns-on","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The rule the whole thing turns on"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Static goes to a class at build time; dynamic goes through a typed custom"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"property."}]},{"t":"text","text":" No class is ever assembled in the browser."}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"// tone is an axis: five rules the emitter already wrote.","kind":"comment"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"when","kind":"function"},{"text":"(tone.danger, [","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"set","kind":"function"},{"text":"(v.bg, palette.accent.danger)]);","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"// a width that depends on a signal cannot be a class — there is no finite set","kind":"comment"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"// of widths to emit — so it goes through a registered <percentage>.","kind":"comment"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"style"},{"text":": ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"function*","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" () {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"return","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"assign","kind":"function"},{"text":"(meterVars.value, unit.","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"pct","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"yield*","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"value","kind":"function"},{"text":"()));","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"}","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"That split is what keeps the set of visual states finite, and therefore"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"enumerable. A class built from a signal is a state nothing recorded."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Where to go next"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Start with "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/style/setup","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Activating "},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/style"}]},{"t":"text","text":": the system is a build"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"step, and none of the pages below produce a single byte of CSS until the Vite"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"plugin is wired. Then "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/style/define","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Define your design system"}]},{"t":"text","text":", which is where"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"bp"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"palette"},{"t":"text","text":" and the theme variables the other pages spend come from."}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/style/tokens","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Tokens and typed variables"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — level 1."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/style/variants","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Axes and the visual matrix"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — level 2."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/style/obligations","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Context obligations"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — level 3."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/style/testing","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Testing what you built"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — drivers, baselines, exhaustiveness."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/style/contrast","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Text contrast"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — WCAG AA proven from the sheets and the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"templates, with no browser, and an explicit list of what it does not cover."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A working example lives in the demo, at"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"apps/demo/src/app/examples/design-system/"},{"t":"text","text":", with a README that walks through"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the same three levels in code."}]}],"outline":[{"level":2,"id":"the-rule-the-whole-thing-turns-on","text":"The rule the whole thing turns on"},{"level":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next"}]}